# Settings for the round keeper. Copy to a file outside the repository (or to a git-ignored .env.keeper.local),
# fill it in locally, chmod 600 it and pass it with --secrets. Only that file is read: the process environment is
# not, and a file that is a symbolic link, larger than 16 KB or not mode 0600 is refused (KEEPER_SECRET_PERMISSIONS).
# Do not paste actual credentials into this tracked example.

# The dedicated wallet: a plain key used by nothing else, funded on Base and on Horizen. The address must be the key's.
KEEPER_ADDRESS=replace-with-dedicated-wallet-address
KEEPER_PRIVATE_KEY=replace-locally

# Where the signed BTC/USD price reports come from.
#   solana     free: the copies of the Chainlink Data Streams reports that public Solana transactions carry. No account.
#   chainlink  the paid Data Streams API, with the two credential lines below.
# Without this line the keeper uses chainlink. Either way the Base adapter must accept a report in simulation first.
KEEPER_REPORT_SOURCE=solana

# Optional with KEEPER_REPORT_SOURCE=solana: an https Solana endpoint replacing the public default
# https://api.mainnet-beta.solana.com (shared, about one call per second per method).
# KEEPER_SOLANA_RPC_URL=

# Data Streams credentials entitled to the BTC/USD stream. Required with KEEPER_REPORT_SOURCE=chainlink. Optional with
# solana: set both and the paid API stands behind the copies (a boundary none has served 60 s after it).
# CHAINLINK_STREAMS_USERNAME=replace-locally
# CHAINLINK_STREAMS_SECRET=replace-locally

# Required. The most each chain may cost in any rolling 24 hours, in wei. It refills by itself; one transaction may
# reserve at most 1/20 of it. Upper bounds: 250000000000000000 (Base), 50000000000000000 (Horizen).
KEEPER_BASE_DAILY_BUDGET_WEI=20000000000000000
KEEPER_HORIZEN_DAILY_BUDGET_WEI=4000000000000000

# Optional https endpoints replacing the public defaults (recommended, and for production in effect required: the
# public ones are shared and rate limited). Each must serve eth_getTransactionReceipt, or the keeper waits with
# KEEPER_RPC_RECEIPTS and sends nothing on that chain. The public Base default does not; while KEEPER_BASE_RPC_URL
# is unset, Base receipts are read from the endpoint the profile names for them (chains.base.receiptRpcUrl in
# contracts/deployment/hybrid-mainnet.json, currently https://mainnet.base.org).
# KEEPER_BASE_RPC_URL=
# KEEPER_HORIZEN_RPC_URL=

# With --rehearsal only: both URLs above are then required and must be http://127.0.0.1:<port> or
# http://localhost:<port> forks, and the report service may be a local stand-in. Ignored without --rehearsal.
# KEEPER_STREAMS_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:<port>

# Optional: the order-book lane (README "Order-book lane"), --watch only. A 0600 file holding 0x and 64 hex: a Horizen
# wallet used for nothing else (never the key above), funded with about 0.005 ETH on Horizen. Without it the lane is off.
# KEEPER_VELA_KEY_FILE=/Users/<you>/.config/zedge/keeper-vela.key
# With --rehearsal only: a fork's order-book manifest instead of the committed one.
# KEEPER_ORDERBOOK_MANIFEST=
